{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(3D_Coordinate_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (3D Coordinate Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(cheap)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (cheap)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four cubes with edge lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are stacked as shown. What is the length of the portion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/95915f5885ed19f737ac8338c7c0b1d0e23fb73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XY}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> contained in the cube with edge length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41120e351bda42fada2fe2803e19a131bc30b96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] dotfactor = 3; size(10cm); dot((0, 10)); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, (0,10),W,fontsize(8pt)); dot((6,2)); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, (6,2),E,fontsize(8pt)); draw((0, 0)--(0, 10)--(1, 10)--(1, 9)--(2, 9)--(2, 7)--(3, 7)--(3,4)--(4, 4)--(4, 0)--cycle); draw((0,9)--(1, 9)--(1.5, 9.5)--(1.5, 10.5)--(0.5, 10.5)--(0, 10)); draw((1, 10)--(1.5,10.5)); draw((1.5, 10)--(3,10)--(3,8)--(2,7)--(0,7)); draw((2,9)--(3,10)); draw((3,8.5)--(4.5,8.5)--(4.5,5.5)--(3,4)--(0,4)); draw((3,7)--(4.5,8.5)); draw((4.5,6)--(6,6)--(6,2)--(4,0)); draw((4,4)--(6,6)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,9.5), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, (2,8), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (3,5.5), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, (4,2), W,fontsize(8pt)); [/asy]\" width=\"308\" height=\"475\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f22d5c260c68925451cf6ea13efd2c6d6c4db7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{33}}5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{33}}3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"472\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Pythagorean Theorem in three dimensions, the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663ca06b65c787bb57267dac72171bd0019c8e87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4^2+4^2+10^2}=2\\sqrt{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Let the length of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> that is inside the cube with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. By similar triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512c0dd3c0c70fa4c9bb74739e1303902b1fcebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{3}=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{33}}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"41\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9d08359ae71c783aaec4663c872d663dafa577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\dfrac{3\\sqrt{33}}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"128\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.283D_Coordinate_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(3D_Coordinate_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (3D Coordinate Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (3D Coordinate Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's redraw the diagram, however make a 3D coordinate plane, using D as the origin.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26d45a4b5b55aa7a59dcd355353f8ce6476fd3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] dotfactor = 3; size(10cm); dot((0, 10)); label(&quot;$X(0,10,0)$&quot;, (0,10),W,fontsize(8pt)); dot((6,2)); label(&quot;$Y(4,0,4)$&quot;, (6,2),E,fontsize(8pt)); draw((0, 0)--(0, 10)--(1, 10)--(1, 9)--(2, 9)--(2, 7)--(3, 7)--(3,4)--(4, 4)--(4, 0)--cycle); draw((0,9)--(1, 9)--(1.5, 9.5)--(1.5, 10.5)--(0.5, 10.5)--(0, 10)); draw((1, 10)--(1.5,10.5)); draw((1.5, 10)--(3,10)--(3,8)--(2,7)--(0,7)); draw((2,9)--(3,10)); draw((3,8.5)--(4.5,8.5)--(4.5,5.5)--(3,4)--(0,4)); draw((3,7)--(4.5,8.5)); draw((4.5,6)--(6,6)--(6,2)--(4,0)); draw((4,4)--(6,6)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,9.5), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, (2,8), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (3,5.5), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, (4,2), W,fontsize(8pt)); label(&quot;$D(0,0,0)$&quot;, (0,0), W,fontsize(8pt)); [/asy]\" width=\"398\" height=\"475\" />\n</p><p>Now we can use the distance formula in 3D, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249de22dd8b835ab18fcab444f6623b46c513199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x_{1}-x_{2})^2+(y_{1}-y_{2})^2+(z_{1}-z_{2})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"296\" height=\"35\" /> and plug it in for the distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e57ce6468d150f4100de86133148c9a11321d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(0-4)^2+(10-0)^2+(0-4)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"259\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>We get the answer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/7588e8129d9e0cea5fea16084cefd0c62ea26a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{132} = 2\\sqrt{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Continuing with solution 1, using similar triangles, we get the answer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/818e14938b28cf15e2c69c9f04bf9e43631e40a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{33}}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~ghfhgvghj10\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagonal of the base of the cube with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e91088fd90499091ba7407f9caef5fa15fc4aa03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Hence by similarity:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5d0893754ce96bc5c7701c74b3c28083cef7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = \\sqrt{3^2 + \\left(\\frac{3}{10} \\cdot 4 \\sqrt{2} \\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{225}{25} + \\frac{6^2 \\cdot 2}{25}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{99 \\cdot 3}}{5} = \\boxed{ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{33}}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"520\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28cheap.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(cheap)\">Solution 4 (cheap)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (cheap)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you don't find any of the solutions above, you can solve the problem in 2D, by considering squares of side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The total length of the line will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed44e017831d0e829b54c8e4200c2363f7306766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4^2 + 10^2} = 2\\sqrt{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />. Using similar triangles, we get that the length of the segment through the square with side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/5062dc70d1e07e570ecfff69febddf3360924efa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{29}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"43\" />. Alternatively, note that this length is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a64112558477bf48ef0786cf050b72465385c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{1 + 2 + 3 + 4}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{29} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{29}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"235\" height=\"45\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1c9d1b1e9b85d185f077bab73eb0531dd6f2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />, the only option with a denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, is likely to be the correct answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the bottom most point on the vertical of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and consider right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450a416ea65cd89b2dd9fe599962f41480ad38fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XPY$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, who has hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdd4f1b83751ff367d78204f7bf502307068f8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" /> It follows that the rations within all cubes are equivalent. The smallest of them has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92cb1e8d1de729875f2842af30d2349f5d422e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10r = 2\\sqrt{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c45b4b468dabc67a71a6ff9d11d6fa5b0190470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{\\sqrt{33}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"43\" />. It follows the segment contained within the cube of volume 27 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842743bb2d6bbffc207daeb044134ba4957bdec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3r = \\boxed{\\frac{3\\sqrt{33}}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"102\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>The motivation for considering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> occurs from the homothety of all such right triangles similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450a416ea65cd89b2dd9fe599962f41480ad38fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XPY$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> at respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of intervals along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255140b38e3c950b5b5927eb6b6a72245cfaa7be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> of lengths 1, 2, 3, 4 respectively, thus the ration <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f842e334458884464891840f6aa26fd934e0d313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2:3:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4FInNJ9wM6s\">https://youtu.be/4FInNJ9wM6s</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 A